  "query_preview": "..\n\n\nKEY MESSAGES:\n\n-  Mild temperatures continue through Thursday.\n\n-  Unsettled weather and cooler temperatures arrive Friday into\n   next weekend.\n\nMild weather will continue across the Northern Rockies through the middle\nof the week. Forecast models show a low pressure system stalling off the\nCalifornia coast by Monday, while the main storm track stays far to the\nnorth across Alaska and northern Canada. This will bring mild daytime\ntemperatures, around 10 degrees above average, across the region. Most\nareas will remain dry today (Sunday) and Monday. However, a few showers are\npossible in north-central Idaho and southwest Montana on Tuesday and\nWednesday as moisture moves north from the California coast.\n\nComputer models show varying solutions as a large low pressure system over\nAlaska and Canada moves south toward the Western U.S. Thursday and Friday.\nMost models suggest this system will combine with the low pressure area off\nthe California coast, increasing the chance for rain and snow by Friday.\nWhile the exact track of these low pressure systems remains uncertain,\nconfidence in a cooler and wetter pattern is high. By the end of the week,\nafternoon temperatures will be 10 to 20 degrees cooler than this weekend,\nreturning to near normal for this time of year.",
